    rank 6-10   excess +3.3|+2.7 pts/yr   win 70% of 40
    rank 11-20  excess +6.3|+4.3 pts/yr   win 92% of 37
    rank 21-50  excess +4.2|+2.9 pts/yr   win 86% of 28
    head-to-head same-window (no averaging artifact): #1 beat the 11-20 book in 11/37 (30%), the 2-5 book did in 20/37 (54%) — >50% = the top of the list is genuinely better than its middle
    head-to-head vs the 6-10 book (#135): #1 beat it in 21/40 (52%), the 2-5 book did in 26/40 (65%) — denominator 40 here vs 37 for the 11-20 line above
  after-tax (28% PT, top-10 book): never-sell +12.2%/yr vs yearly-rotation +10.5%/yr -> deferral edge +1.7 pts/yr
  (BOOK = equal-weight terminal wealth annualized (winners carry it, a zero costs its 1/N weight); >0 beats S&P500.
