Caveats:
  • Peer-relative (#1): returns are de-meaned per ~6mo cutoff, so rho is SELECTION vs same-period
    peers (regime beta removed). A near-empty bucket has a weak peer set -> its rows count for less.
  • In-sample: knobs were hand-tuned on today's data; even the OOS split shares the regime.
  • Survivorship (#6 STRESS ON): crashed/delisted losers were INJECTED into the pool, so this
    run partly corrects the upward bias. Compare its rho/edge to a plain run: a big drop = the
    edge leaned on survivors; holding up (both OOS halves still +) = the edge is real.
  • Price-only (#6): no as-of P/E reconstructed, so the `value` multiplier is ×1.0 here; as-of DIVIDENDS are live since #53 and every dividend row below is real.
  • Overlapping 6-mo windows share price paths -> samples aren't independent; rho is directional.
  • Long-horizon (MAX monthly): only names alive for the FULL 12y window enter, so
    survivorship bias is WORSE than the daily path, and vol/MA are monthly-bar approximations.
backtest: STRESS — injecting 12 crashed/delisted losers (any Yahoo no longer serves are skipped)
backtest: 212 tickers, WALK-FORWARD scoring every ~6mo with a 12y forward holdout each (MAX monthly history)…